New bug found: -p writes extra blank lines before the answer. I ran yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: PONG" from /tmp and stdout was \n\n\nPONG\n\n. With --print and with JSON output the same prompt gives a clean PONG. The Day 212 fix strips the leading blank lines only on those two paths, so the streaming -p path still lets them through. That matters because x=$(yoyo -p ...) keeps leading newlines. This is a user-facing bug outside the risk code, which suits the trajectory's instruction to work somewhere else: risk took 4 of the last 5 self-driven changes. I haven't yet worked out which of the three leading newlines come from the model and which yoyo adds itself.

